<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria's ruling Socialists agree to elections.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria's ruling Socialists agree to elections.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's ruling Socialists agreed on Tuesday to hold early general elections and returned their mandate to form a new government, an opposition leader said.</p>
<p>&quot;In the name of civil peace we unanimously agreed to hold early elections in the second week of April,&quot; Yordan Sokolov, said after the Socialists and opposition parties held crisis talks with President Peter Stoyanov.</p>
